And once again, my greatest enemy proves to be my own stupidity.

My descent from the Mines entrance was largely uneventful until I hit 
the Big Room (oval variety). I was *not* ready for a monster group that 
large, so I picked up the two wands near the upstair (later determined 
that these were striking) and zapped a /oDig that I'd found earlier. 
Kept going down, ran into a level with a mind flayer on it. Went 
looking for it the hard way--should've put on that towel I was carrying 
to find it via telepathy. Found a treasure zoo before I dound the 
flayer, so I cleared it out. Later ran into the *invisible* mind flayer 
and foolishly tried to melee it--again, should've put on that towel, 
after making an E-graving to stand on. Only lost two INT, which a 
previously-liberated unicorn horn restored, and no important IDs.

Eventually, I hit Medusa's Island (titan version, and I was thanking 
Tyr that it was peaceful). Now, after dispatching the gremlin, I 
actually saved and took a break--partly to figure out how to get across 
the water (use that ring of levitation--duh), partly to avoid doing 
something stupid. As the title suggests, I was only successful with the 
former. Surprisingly, it wasn't an eel or such that did me in; I 
actually remembered that towel by this point and used it to avoid all 
the sea critters. No, it was a baluchitherium on the rightmost island 
(the one with a boulder in the dead end). That was pretty much a garden 
variety YASD; I tried to melee it and wasn't watching my HP. Again, I 
shpuld've droppedsome stuff, taken off the ring, and--you guessed it--
made an E-graving.

Oh well, some lessons learned, and now I have a new marker for 
progress.


